ion","i-lucide-settings",{"title":194,"path":195,"stem":196,"icon":26},"Organization Management","\u002Fplatform\u002Forganization-management","03.platform\u002F04.organization-management",{"title":198,"path":199,"stem":200,"icon":201},"System Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsystem-security","03.platform\u002F05.system-security","i-lucide-shield",{"title":203,"path":204,"stem":205,"icon":47},"Defense in Depth","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdefense-in-depth","03.platform\u002F06.defense-in-depth",{"title":207,"path":208,"stem":209,"icon":210},"MCP Tools","\u002Fplatform\u002Fmcp-tools","03.platform\u002F07.mcp-tools","i-lucide-bot",{"title":212,"path":213,"stem":214,"icon":215},"Observability","\u002Fplatform\u002Fobservability","03.platform\u002F08.observability","i-lucide-activity",{"title":217,"path":218,"stem":219,"icon":220},"Contributing","\u002Fplatform\u002Fcontributing","03.platform\u002F09.contributing","i-lucide-git-pull-request",{"title":222,"path":223,"stem":224,"icon":225},"System Migrations","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsystem-migrations","03.platform\u002F10.system-migrations","i-lucide-database-zap",{"title":227,"path":228,"stem":229,"icon":230},"Service Call Liveness","\u002Fplatform\u002Fservice-call-liveness","03.platform\u002F11.service-call-liveness","i-lucide-heart-pulse",{"title":160,"icon":161,"path":232,"stem":233,"children":234,"page":23},"\u002Fplatform\u002Freference","03.platform\u002F12.reference",[235,240,245,249],{"title":236,"path":237,"stem":238,"icon":239},"CRI Format","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fcri-format","03.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format","i-lucide-link",{"title":241,"path":242,"stem":243,"icon":244},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","03.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":246,"path":247,"stem":248,"icon":183},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","03.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":250,"path":251,"stem":252,"icon":36},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","03.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":254,"path":255,"stem":256,"icon":257},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","03.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":259,"path":260,"stem":261,"icon":262},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","03.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":264,"path":265,"stem":266,"icon":267},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","03.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":269,"title":68,"body":270,"description":557,"extension":558,"links":559,"meta":560,"navigation":561,"path":69,"seo":562,"stem":70,"__hash__":563},"docs\u002F02.organizations\u002F03.apps\u002F01.application-structure\u002F03.artifact-types.md",{"type":271,"value":272,"toc":547},"minimark",[273,282,286,289,294,318,323,334,337,341,348,352,360,364,379,382,386,389,393,401,405,413,417,420,424,429,433,438,442,445,449,454,458,466,470,473,544],[274,275,276,277,281],"p",{},"Every project in a Kinotic application contributes one or more ",[278,279,280],"strong",{},"artifacts",". An artifact is a typed output that the platform knows how to build, deploy, and manage. This page describes each artifact type and when to use it.",[283,284,93],"h2",{"id":285},"persistence",[274,287,288],{},"The most common starting point. A persistence artifact defines your domain models (entities) and gets auto-generated CRUD services in return.",[274,290,291],{},[278,292,293],{},"What you provide:",[295,296,297],"ul",{},[298,299,300,301,305,306,309,310,313,314,317],"li",{},"Entity classes decorated with ",[302,303,304],"code",{},"@Entity"," and field-level annotations like ",[302,307,308],{},"@NotNull",", ",[302,311,312],{},"@Precision",", and ",[302,315,316],{},"@AutoGeneratedId",".",[274,319,320],{},[278,321,322],{},"What the platform provides:",[295,324,325,328,331],{},[298,326,327],{},"Full CRUD operations (save, find, delete) with pagination and sorting.",[298,329,330],{},"Named queries derived from method naming conventions.",[298,332,333],{},"Automatic storage provisioning and indexing.",[274,335,336],{},"Persistence is typically the first artifact you create because it establishes the data model that the rest of the application builds on.",[283,338,340],{"id":339},"microservice","Microservice",[274,342,343,344,317],{},"A microservice artifact is long-running code that executes in a pod or VM. It publishes services that other parts of the application can discover and call through ",[345,346,347],"a",{"href":86},"service proxies",[274,349,350],{},[278,351,293],{},[295,353,354,357],{},[298,355,356],{},"TypeScript classes that implement your business logic.",[298,358,359],{},"Service interfaces that you want to expose to the rest of the application.",[274,361,362],{},[278,363,322],{},[295,365,366,369,376],{},[298,367,368],{},"Automatic service registration in the Service Directory.",[298,370,371,372,375],{},"Service discovery and zone-based routing so other projects can call your service through a ",[345,373,374],{"href":86},"service proxy"," with a simple function call.",[298,377,378],{},"Lifecycle management, scaling, and health monitoring.",[274,380,381],{},"Use a microservice when your logic goes beyond simple CRUD -- orchestrating across multiple entities, calling external APIs, or running long-lived workflows.",[283,383,385],{"id":384},"batch-job","Batch Job",[274,387,388],{},"A batch job artifact is code that runs on a schedule. It is ideal for periodic tasks like data aggregation, report generation, cleanup routines, or syncing with external systems.",[274,390,391],{},[278,392,293],{},[295,394,395,398],{},[298,396,397],{},"TypeScript code that performs the job.",[298,399,400],{},"A schedule definition (cron expression or interval).",[274,402,403],{},[278,404,322],{},[295,406,407,410],{},[298,408,409],{},"Scheduled execution with retry and failure handling.",[298,411,412],{},"Logging and observability for each run.",[283,414,416],{"id":415},"ui-component","UI Component",[274,418,419],{},"A UI component artifact produces reusable building blocks that can be shared across multiple frontends within the application. Think of it as an internal component library.",[274,421,422],{},[278,423,293],{},[295,425,426],{},[298,427,428],{},"Reusable UI components packaged for consumption by frontend projects.",[274,430,431],{},[278,432,322],{},[295,434,435],{},[298,436,437],{},"Versioning and distribution within the application.",[283,439,441],{"id":440},"frontend","Frontend",[274,443,444],{},"A frontend artifact is a complete user interface that gets deployed as a static site. It consumes services published by other projects in the application.",[274,446,447],{},[278,448,293],{},[295,450,451],{},[298,452,453],{},"A web application (built with any framework) that compiles to static assets.",[274,455,456],{},[278,457,322],{},[295,459,460,463],{},[298,461,462],{},"Static hosting with CDN distribution.",[298,464,465],{},"Automatic connection to the application's services through the Kinotic client libraries.",[283,467,469],{"id":468},"combining-artifact-types","Combining Artifact Types",[274,471,472],{},"Most real-world applications combine several artifact types. A typical setup might look like this:",[474,475,476,492],"table",{},[477,478,479],"thead",{},[480,481,482,486,489],"tr",{},[483,484,485],"th",{},"Project",[483,487,488],{},"Artifact Type",[483,490,491],{},"Role",[493,494,495,508,520,532],"tbody",{},[480,496,497,503,505],{},[498,499,500],"td",{},[302,501,502],{},"data",[498,504,93],{},[498,506,507],{},"Defines entities and provides auto-generated CRUD services",[480,509,510,515,517],{},[498,511,512],{},[302,513,514],{},"services",[498,516,340],{},[498,518,519],{},"Implements business rules that orchestrate across entities",[480,521,522,527,529],{},[498,523,524],{},[302,525,526],{},"jobs",[498,528,385],{},[498,530,531],{},"Runs nightly data aggregation",[480,533,534,539,541],{},[498,535,536],{},[302,537,538],{},"web",[498,540,441],{},[498,542,543],{},"The main user interface",[274,545,546],{},"Each project is independently developed and versioned, but they all deploy as part of the same application and communicate through the Service Directory.",{"title":548,"searchDepth":549,"depth":549,"links":550},"",2,[551,552,553,554,555,556],{"id":285,"depth":549,"text":93},{"id":339,"depth":549,"text":340},{"id":384,"depth":549,"text":385},{"id":415,"depth":549,"text":416},{"id":440,"depth":549,"text":441},{"id":468,"depth":549,"text":469},"Learn about the different artifact types a Kinotic project can contribute -- from persistence and microservices to frontends.","md",null,{},true,{"title":68,"description":557},"ESZKcYK7bCPSg-cL430qPTXSA0ZdBewKNTGCB04a2a0",[565,567],{"title":64,"path":65,"stem":66,"description":566,"children":-1},"Learn how to configure Kinotic applications and the projects that compose them.",{"title":31,"path":78,"stem":79,"description":568,"children":-1},"How services work in Kinotic and the communication patterns they support.",1792930938646]